A2-B  does OracleTruncated fire before a wrong answer can be returned?
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  budget 10 (solvable): full search -> solvable=True in 120 nodes
     node_limit=1      -> OracleTruncated (refused to answer)
     node_limit=5      -> OracleTruncated (refused to answer)
     node_limit=20     -> OracleTruncated (refused to answer)
     node_limit=60     -> OracleTruncated (refused to answer)
     node_limit=119    -> OracleTruncated (refused to answer)
     node_limit=120    -> solvable=True nodes=120
  budget 9 (unsolvable): full search -> solvable=False in 119 nodes
     node_limit=1      -> OracleTruncated (refused to answer)
     node_limit=5      -> OracleTruncated (refused to answer)
     node_limit=20     -> OracleTruncated (refused to answer)
     node_limit=60     -> OracleTruncated (refused to answer)
     node_limit=118    -> OracleTruncated (refused to answer)
     node_limit=119    -> solvable=False nodes=119

A2-C  is the counter really unread when no step_limit is declared?
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   self.commands = 0          # commands since the last RESET, RESET excluded
   self.commands = 0
   self.commands += 1
   if self.commands > op["limit"]:
   "commands": self.commands,
   -> the only read is the step_limit comparison; the only writes are the
      RESET zeroing and the pre-step_limit increment.
